  {
    "id": "adya-art-of-inquiry",
    "content": "True self-inquiry is not asking yourself questions and looking for answers within the mind. It is resting in not knowing and allowing the truth to reveal itself.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "The Art of Self-Inquiry",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["self-inquiry", "surrender"],
    "moodTags": ["morning", "contemplative"],
    "type": "article",
    "sourceUrl": "https://adyashanti.opengatesangha.org/teachings/library/writing/subject/10"
  },
  {
    "id": "adya-doorway-i-am",
    "content": "The doorway of \"I Am\" is the entry point to the infinite. When you rest in the sense of \"I Am\" without adding anything to it, you discover your true nature.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "The Doorway of \"I Am\"",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["self-inquiry", "awareness", "nature"],
    "moodTags": ["contemplative"],
    "type": "article",
    "sourceUrl": "https://adyashanti.opengatesangha.org/teachings/library/writing/subject/10"
  },
  {
    "id": "adya-inner-revolution",
    "content": "An inner revolution is not a political act. It is the most intimate act of all\u2014the willingness to question every belief you have ever held about yourself and reality.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "An Inner Revolution",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["awareness", "self-inquiry", "truth"],
    "moodTags": ["challenging"],
    "type": "article",
    "sourceUrl": "https://adyashanti.opengatesangha.org/teachings/library/writing/subject/10"
  },
  {
    "id": "adya-paradox-true-nature",
    "content": "Embracing the paradox of true nature means accepting that you are both nothing and everything, empty and full, separate and inseparable.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "Embracing the Paradox of True Nature",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["awareness", "truth", "nature"],
    "moodTags": ["contemplative"],
    "type": "article",
    "sourceUrl": "https://adyashanti.opengatesangha.org/teachings/library/writing/subject/10"
  },
  {
    "id": "adya-awe-wonder",
    "content": "The awe and wonder of existence is always available. It is not something to be achieved but something to be noticed. Right now, existence is happening.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "The Awe and Wonder of Existence",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["awareness", "life", "presence"],
    "moodTags": ["uplifting", "morning"],
    "type": "article",
    "sourceUrl": "https://adyashanti.opengatesangha.org/teachings/library/writing/subject/10"
  },
  {
    "id": "adya-relationship",
    "content": "In relationship, we have the opportunity to see ourselves clearly. The other person becomes a mirror, reflecting back to us what we have not yet seen in ourselves.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "Relationship",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["relationship", "awareness"],
    "moodTags": ["general"],
    "type": "article",
    "sourceUrl": "https://adyashanti.opengatesangha.org/teachings/library/writing/subject/2"
  },
  {
    "id": "adya-spiritual-life",
    "content": "What is a spiritual life? It is not about becoming someone special. It is about becoming more and more ordinary, more and more simple, more and more present.",
    "teacher": "Adyashanti",
    "source": "What Is a Spiritual Life?",
    "lineage": "contemporary",
    "topicTags": ["life", "practice", "presence"],
    "moodTags": ["morning", "general"],
    "type": "article",
